Subject: [PATCH 08/17] =?UTF-8?q?Add=20F6=E2=80=93F10=20and=20Muhenkan=20k?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ey=20support=20for=20kana=20commit=20shortcuts?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements the standard Japanese IME F-key shortcuts and the Muhenkan key
in both Composing and Conversion states:

- F6: commit as hiragana
- F7: commit as full-width katakana
- F8: commit as half-width katakana
- F9: commit typed romaji as full-width ASCII (no lossy reverse conversion)
- F10: commit typed romaji as half-width ASCII
- Muhenkan (無変換): toggle hiragana/katakana in Composing; commit as
  full-width katakana in Conversion

F9/F10 reconstruct the original typed romaji via `raw_inputs: Vec<String>`,
a Vec parallel to `input_buf.text` where `raw_inputs[i]` holds the romaji
that produced char `i`. This avoids the information loss of hiragana→romaji
reverse conversion and correctly handles cursor movement, mid-buffer edits,
Ctrl+Space, and multi-kana digraph groups (e.g. "kya"→"きゃ").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
